From 515503ee9b9b9d9e6555a1d651d60845ae6f5592 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 22:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Podcast: paste-text + batch series generation, fix
 contentDraftId/knowledgeAssetId mismatch

- lib/podcastGenerate.js: shared script->TTS->segments pipeline, extracted
  from generate/route.js so every entry point reuses it
- generate/route.js: now stores knowledge_asset_id on the episode (was
  content_draft_id: null), supports raw_content assets, adds maxDuration=60
- generate-from-text/route.js (new): pasted/playbook text or a blog post's
  own content -> one episode. Saves pasted text as a knowledge_asset for
  traceability; blog posts skip that (saveAsAsset: false) since
  content_drafts is already their source of truth
- generate-batch/route.js (new): long text -> LLM-split into an episode
  series. Runs as an async background job (lib/backgroundTask.js,
  mirroring the books.generation_status pattern) since a full series can
  run well past a request's time budget. New status/route.js is polled by
  the paste-text page
- AdminGeneratePodcastButton.js: was sending contentDraftId to a route that
  only accepts knowledgeAssetId, so this button never actually worked on
  the blog admin page. Now posts the post's own title/content to
  generate-from-text directly
- app/admin/blog/page.js: pass title/content instead of contentDraftId
- app/admin/podcasts/paste/page.js (new): paste-text UI, single episode or
  batch series, target-minutes input, polls batch status
- app/admin/podcasts/page.js: link to the new paste page, groups episodes
  by series_id, fixes regenerateEpisode using the now-stored
  knowledge_asset_id
- migration 20260801_podcast_manual_batch.sql: knowledge_assets gets
  raw_content + source; podcast_episodes gets knowledge_asset_id/series_id/
  series_title/episode_number; new podcast_batch_jobs table for the async
  batch status
